See which shortcuts you use most, explore when you type and click, and turn a day or a week of activity into a shareable report.

{access}## Downloads

Choose a package for your system below.

{downloads}
## What’s new

- **Shortcuts.** See your most-used shortcuts and look up their common uses in the [Shortcut Atlas](https://endnone.github.io/ClickPulse/). On macOS and Windows, shortcut recognition follows the active keyboard layout for supported character keys.
- **Reports.** Create a daily report or a weekly report covering the last seven days by default. You can also choose a range of 2–31 days. Save the card as a PNG, copy the image on macOS or Windows, or copy a prompt to design your own poster.
- **History and heatmaps.** Compare hourly keyboard and mouse activity by weekday, zoom in on a time range, and see which physical mouse buttons you use most.

## Upgrading on macOS

If you’re upgrading from 0.3.1 or earlier, open **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Input Monitoring**. Remove the old ClickPulse entry, then add the updated app and enable it. Future versions signed with the same certificate should keep this permission. Updating keeps your history and settings.

The Mac app uses a fixed self-signed certificate and hasn’t been notarized by Apple. The Windows app is unsigned.

